+"""PREREG_V8F_TFAR launch gate: ``tfar_check.py`` (argv, gate, post identity, token, runner). A fake tree, fake data and a fake trainer: no model training, no GPU. Pattern of ``test_ckpt120_check.py``.
+
+Every check has a deliberate-regression arm (a MUTATION that must turn the gate RED): each ``tfar_probe`` key (the value it must read: non-zero where the lever is on, EXACTLY 0.0 for each control), each argv lever, the built-lever rule
+(a key present with the lever OFF is a defect: the roundabout patch's always-present ``nav_rb`` key broke 7 tests), each token binding, the post identity (the layer must leave its zero init, TZ's weight must NOT) and G-EVAL.
